The key fix: all occurrences of `jsonPath("$.csrf").optional().saveAs("staleCsrf")` have been changed to `jsonPath("$.csrf").optional().saveAs("csrf")`. This ensures that when a fresh CSRF token is returned by any response (including session renewal), it properly updates the `csrf` session variable that is used by all subsequent authenticated requests via the `X-CSRF-Token` header.

